RetroChat for NetBSD 10.1/mac68k
================================

This package contains architecture-independent Tcl source and a NetBSD shell
launcher. It is intended for NetBSD 10.1 on Motorola 680x0 Macintosh systems.

The server requires Tcl 8.0 or newer. The client requires Tcl/Tk 8.0 or newer
and a working X11 display. The installer ISO bundles the complete Tcl/Tk 8.6
m68k runtime and installs it automatically when it is not already available.

Run the client with ./retrochat-client and the server with
./retrochat-server 7777. The launchers use tclsh/wish from PATH, then try
/usr/pkg/bin. These packages do not bundle Tcl/Tk or native machine code.

The installer ISO includes INSTALL.SH, which installs both packages and creates
/usr/local/bin/retrochat-client and /usr/local/bin/retrochat-server launchers.
No separate package download or pkgsrc build is required.

When the server is launched under X11, it uses a quit-only status controller.
Tk 8.x does not provide a native system-tray API, so this is a small window.
With no DISPLAY, the same launcher runs the headless server with tclsh.
On a one-bit X display, both graphical applications use black text on white.
